### ===================================================================
### Distributed Job Scheduler - IntelliJ HTTP Client Requests
### You can click the green "Run / Play" icon next to any request below!
### ===================================================================

### 1. Create a Project
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ECommerce-Platform",
  "description": "Primary background job processing project"
}

### 2. List All Projects
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/projects

### 3. Create a Queue for the Project
# Replace projectId with the ID returned from Step 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/queues
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "PASTE_PROJECT_ID_HERE",
  "name": "email-queue",
  "priority": 10,
  "concurrencyLimit": 5
}

### 4. List Queues
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/queues

### 5. Submit a SEND_EMAIL Job (Immediate Execution)
# Replace projectId and queueId with IDs from Step 1 and Step 3
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "PASTE_PROJECT_ID_HERE",
  "queueId": "PASTE_QUEUE_ID_HERE",
  "jobType": "SEND_EMAIL",
  "payload": {
    "to": "developer@company.org",
    "subject": "Hello from Distributed Job Scheduler!",
    "body": "This job was triggered from IntelliJ IDEA."
  },
  "priority": 10
}

### 6. Get Job Details by ID
# Replace jobId with the ID returned from Step 5
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/jobs/PASTE_JOB_ID_HERE

### 7. View Job Execution History & Step-by-Step Logs
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/jobs/PASTE_JOB_ID_HERE/executions
